language Hedley version 0.2
status PROPOSED
purpose human_agent_communication

principle compact_by_default
  model only state that changes a decision or guarantee
  keep uncommon detail behind stable references

principle no_silent_semantics
  every claimed outcome must appear in Hedley
  missing expressiveness becomes a language_gap

construct state
  declares domain state and initial values

construct rule
  models an internal transition
  enabled when <guard>
  a false guard means BLOCKED only
  no error or response is implied

construct operation <id>(<inputs>) -> <Outcome>
  models an external invocation
  cases are disjoint and exhaustive

  case <id>
    when <precondition>
    return <Outcome>
    change <state assignments>
    ensure <postcondition>
    preserve <important unchanged state>

construct workflow <id>
  models non-atomic behavior only when intermediate effects matter
  names steps, commit points, failures, interruptions, and recovery

construct adapter <id>
  maps an Outcome to protocol-visible behavior
  may define diagnostics, exit codes, responses, or UI messages
  may not redefine the domain transition

construct invariant <id>
  holds in every reachable state within the declared scope

construct transition_property <id>
  relates pre-state and post-state for named accepted cases

construct language_gap <id>
  claim <behavior not expressible>
  missing_construct <needed semantic feature>
  consequence <what cannot be established>

construct correspondence <id>
  contract <stable Hedley IDs>
  implementation <revision and stable symbols>
  verification <evidence IDs>
  status PROPOSED | SOURCE_INSPECTED | TESTED | MODEL_CHECKED | PROVED

construct evidence <id>
  checked <claim and target>
  method <command, inspection, model, or proof>
  result <observed result>
  limits <scope not established>

protocol conversation
  use Hedley for the selected semantic discussion
  do not substitute English or another language for a missing construct
  reference stable IDs during review and comprehension checks
  expand detail only when it changes a decision, guarantee, or failure model

unknown
  formal grammar
  parser and type checker
  composition between contracts
  temporal and concurrency notation beyond explicit workflows
  editor and visual projection

